# Values that must be identical in the chat harness, the BFF, and the Tool
# Layer, because each one verifies what another signed or sent. Generate each as
# an independent value of at least 32 bytes, for example:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# These two are the only contents of this file. If a secret is not needed by
# all three services, it belongs in that service's own .env instead.
#
# The chat harness signs actor assertions with RELAY_TOOL_ACTOR_SECRET; the
# Tool Layer and the BFF each verify that signature independently. A mismatch
# does not fail at startup - it surfaces as every Gmail call being refused.
RELAY_BFF_CAPABILITY=
RELAY_TOOL_ACTOR_SECRET=